{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:68894f863d6802d1","name":"TC-Series Protocol Droid","source":{"id":"source:reference-68894f863d6802d1","title":"TC-Series Protocol Droid","revision":19044,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T21:11:46Z","sha256":"bda0873035c2982bc1e6770264b742c770855fb6e1b1fd657766f14c5617a01f","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19044","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=TC-Series%20Protocol%20Droid&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-68894f863d6802d1","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threats of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threats_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The TC-Series of Protocol Droids from ",{"tag":"a","children":["Cybot Galactica"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Cybot_Galactica","referenceId":"reference:8d89ff519236e3e2"}," was designed in an attempt to supplant the ",{"tag":"a","children":["3PO-Series"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/3PO-Series_Protocol_Droid","referenceId":"reference:0cbde42806fd4d2c"}," of Protocol Droids. Although successful, the TC-Series never came close to replacing the more famous Protocol Droid model. Unlike the 3PO-Series, the TC-Series includes a TranLang III communications center, a feature that only a few ",{"tag":"a","children":["3PO-Series Protocol Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/3PO-Series_Protocol_Droids"}," could boast. In addition to their enhanced communications equipment, all TC-Series Protocol Droids were designed with the latest technology in nearly every system, and they received a total programming rewrite before the line was launched to ensure that there were no holdover problems from other software packages. \n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["In almost all ways, the TC-Series is one of the most technologically advanced and reliable Protocol Droids on the market. However, its increased price coupled with the longstanding reputation of the 3PO-Series Droids ensured that few people made the switch to the TC-Series Protocol Droid. The TC-Series Droid is popular among wealthy nobles and Senators and is also commonly found aboard Trade Federation ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships"}," (since the Federation has no difficulty in dealing with price issues). Despite the company's hope that the TC-Series would replace the 3PO-Series entirely (thus selling millions of new Droids to beings wishing to upgrade to the TC-Series), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Cybot Galactica"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Cybot_Galactica","referenceId":"reference:8d89ff519236e3e2"}," decided instead to market the TC-Series Droids as a luxury alternative to the 3PO-Series, since sales were solid but nowhere near as high as they would need to be to replace the older Droid model.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["TC-Series Protocol Droids can be played as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Heroes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Heroes"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["TC-Series Droids Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["TC-Series Protocol Droids are most often found in the company of nobles and businessmen who have extra credits to spend on an expensive Protocol Droid. Very few TC-Series Droids make their way into the hands of anyone who is less than wealthy, though it has been known to happen. The TC-Series is very often sought after because of its superior programming, and many wealthy owners use TC-Series Droids as majordomos and personal assistants. Since the TC-Series Protocol Droid has a Heroic Level, it is much more durable than other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"}," and is slightly more survivable. Additionally, its ability to coordinate allies makes it an excellent aide in combat; though it does not contribute anything directly, it can enhance the ability of other characters to work together. \n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["TC-Series Protocol Droid Statistics (CL 1)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["3rd-Degree Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/3rd-Degree_Droid"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Noble"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Noble","referenceId":"reference:190d375ec3483f8f"}," 1\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," -1; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +7\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Binary"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Binary","referenceId":"reference:ee1c8277caf5fb9b"},", 3 Unassigned; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Translator Unit"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Translator_Unit","referenceId":"reference:0bcd4b383b11cac0"}," (DC 5)\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 11 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 11), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 10, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},": 15\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 18, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"},": 10\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","